  "derivation": "Synthetic fixture, the case effects-loads without a model.sections/1 record: no load, assignment or restraint effect reads the section state, so the effects are those derived there. Synthetic fixture. State: patterns DEAD and LIVE; frame load row (B1, DEAD, gravity) w 10 kN/m; area load row (F1, DEAD, gravity) q 2 kPa. c1 puts 12000 N/m on frames B1 and B2 in DEAD: 12000 N/m x 1 / 1000 = 12 kN/m. B1 has the row, so it is a `set` of /w_kN_m on [frame_loads, B1, DEAD, gravity]; B2 has none in that pattern, so it is an `add` of the whole row {frame B2, pattern DEAD, direction gravity, w_kN_m 12}. c2 puts the basis field loads.live_kPa = 3 kPa on area F1 in LIVE: F1 has no LIVE row, so an `add` {area F1, pattern LIVE, direction gravity, q_kPa 3}. c3 puts 2.5 kPa on F1 in DEAD: the row exists, so a `set` of /q_kPa 2.5. Sorted by key: area_loads before frame_loads; within area_loads (F1, DEAD) before (F1, LIVE); within frame_loads B1 before B2. c1 gives two effects: c1/1 (B1) and c1/2 (B2); c2 and c3 keep their ids.",
